1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,662
Late 2024. A data center in Malaysia.

2
00:00:04,981 --> 00:00:09,153
An official from the US Commerce Department is
walking through the building when he

3
00:00:09,153 --> 00:00:10,460
notices something strange.

4
00:00:11,451 --> 00:00:17,059
Stacks of boxes. Brand-new Nvidia AI chips. Some
of the most wanted computer chips

5
00:00:17,059 --> 00:00:18,016
on the planet.

6
00:00:19,178 --> 00:00:20,320
And they are still sealed.

7
00:00:21,643 --> 00:00:26,387
If you buy chips this powerful for your own data
center, you open them. You plug

8
00:00:26,387 --> 00:00:27,691
them in. You use them.

9
00:00:29,046 --> 00:00:33,225
Unless they were never meant to stay there...

10
00:00:33,545 --> 00:00:37,601
According to reports, that one moment helped start
an investigation that would reach

11
00:00:37,601 --> 00:00:41,513
a mysterious Chinese businesswoman, the White
House, and the man running the most

12
00:00:41,513 --> 00:00:43,251
important tech company in the world.

13
00:00:44,040 --> 00:00:44,700
Jensen Huang.

14
00:00:46,106 --> 00:00:48,296
Within two years, he would lose his job.

15
00:00:49,170 --> 00:00:51,282
And just ten days later... get it back.

16
00:00:52,593 --> 00:00:57,520
This is the story of how it happened. And why,
even now, nobody can say for sure

17
00:00:57,520 --> 00:00:58,629
what the truth is.

18
00:00:59,786 --> 00:01:00,655
Let's open the file.

19
00:01:02,251 --> 00:01:05,070
To understand this story, you need to understand
one thing.

20
00:01:06,050 --> 00:01:10,782
Every powerful AI system in the world, from
chatbots to self-driving cars to

21
00:01:10,782 --> 00:01:14,268
military software, needs special chips to train
and run.

22
00:01:15,085 --> 00:01:17,454
And the company that makes most of them is Nvidia.

23
00:01:18,711 --> 00:01:24,437
If AI is a war, Nvidia is the company making the
weapons. For both sides, if it can.

24
00:01:25,567 --> 00:01:30,415
That's why, in October 2022, the US government
banned Nvidia from selling its most

25
00:01:30,415 --> 00:01:31,834
advanced chips to China.

26
00:01:32,994 --> 00:01:37,349
Washington's fear is simple. If China gets ahead
in AI, its military and

27
00:01:37,349 --> 00:01:39,829
surveillance power could grow enormously.

28
00:01:41,157 --> 00:01:45,914
Beijing sees it very differently. To China, these
bans are an attempt to hold back

29
00:01:45,914 --> 00:01:48,003
its economy and keep America on top.

30
00:01:49,219 --> 00:01:53,090
Donald Trump has put it bluntly: whoever wins AI,
wins.

31
00:01:54,238 --> 00:01:56,868
And caught right in the middle of this fight was
one man.

32
00:01:58,065 --> 00:02:02,907
Her name, according to reports, is Alice Huang. No
relation to Jensen, despite the

33
00:02:02,907 --> 00:02:03,675
same surname.

34
00:02:04,672 --> 00:02:08,785
She is a Chinese citizen. And on paper, her career
looks impressive.

35
00:02:09,987 --> 00:02:15,482
According to the Washington Post, she worked as a
journalist at Chinese state TV,

36
00:02:15,482 --> 00:02:20,841
then at major banks, and by around 2015, she was a
senior manager at a Shanghai

37
00:02:20,841 --> 00:02:26,335
private equity firm. The owner of that firm, Kang
Wei, was later described as her

38
00:02:26,335 --> 00:02:26,878
husband.

39
00:02:27,878 --> 00:02:28,833
But here's the problem.

40
00:02:29,511 --> 00:02:34,752
Almost none of it can be independently confirmed.
No public record of the TV work.

41
00:02:34,752 --> 00:02:36,350
No proof of the marriage.

42
00:02:37,108 --> 00:02:42,382
A former top CIA China analyst, Dennis Wilder,
said her background looked like a

43
00:02:42,382 --> 00:02:47,261
"legend." In spy language, that means a fake
identity, built to look real.

44
00:02:48,441 --> 00:02:52,209
So how did she get so close to one of the richest
men in the world?

45
00:02:52,750 --> 00:02:57,961
According to the Wall Street Journal, it was her
own husband who introduced them. He

46
00:02:57,961 --> 00:03:02,987
had known Jensen for years, back when his firm
invested in video games and Nvidia

47
00:03:02,987 --> 00:03:05,034
was mostly a gaming chip company.

48
00:03:05,550 --> 00:03:10,569
Their first public meeting on record was a dinner
in Singapore, in December 2023.

49
00:03:11,599 --> 00:03:16,680
Over the next few years, they were reportedly seen
together in Taipei, in Shanghai,

50
00:03:16,680 --> 00:03:20,597
at Nvidia offices in America, and at golf resorts
in California.

51
00:03:21,510 --> 00:03:25,620
And they weren't exactly hiding. Photos of them
together were posted online.

52
00:03:26,639 --> 00:03:30,120
Keep that detail in mind. It will matter later.

53
00:03:30,816 --> 00:03:34,854
While all this was happening, a company connected
to Alice was quietly growing.

54
00:03:35,532 --> 00:03:37,070
It was called MegaSpeed.

55
00:03:37,984 --> 00:03:43,157
In March 2023, Alice reportedly bought a company
in Singapore and renamed it

56
00:03:43,157 --> 00:03:43,838
MegaSpeed.

57
00:03:44,520 --> 00:03:49,279
Eight months later, her name was removed from the
list of directors. Ownership moved

58
00:03:49,279 --> 00:03:50,355
to a shell company.

59
00:03:51,148 --> 00:03:56,259
And just four days after that, MegaSpeed became an
official Nvidia cloud partner,

60
00:03:56,259 --> 00:03:59,162
which meant priority access to Nvidia's chips.

61
00:04:00,274 --> 00:04:01,230
Now look at the numbers.

62
00:04:01,701 --> 00:04:08,652
In 2023, MegaSpeed's total assets were reportedly
around 33 million dollars.

63
00:04:09,192 --> 00:04:10,231
One year later? Around 3 billion.

64
00:04:10,909 --> 00:04:13,780
That's roughly ninety times bigger, in a single
year.

65
00:04:14,370 --> 00:04:19,285
A sister company in Malaysia reportedly bought at
least 4.8 billion dollars of

66
00:04:19,285 --> 00:04:22,562
advanced AI equipment, almost all of it from
Nvidia.

67
00:04:23,260 --> 00:04:28,716
According to an investigation by The Information,
Alice used her companies, and her

68
00:04:28,716 --> 00:04:34,238
connection to Jensen, to help move at least 5
billion dollars' worth of Nvidia chips

69
00:04:34,238 --> 00:04:35,618
to Chinese companies.

70
00:04:36,417 --> 00:04:41,735
And according to Bloomberg, at least 500 chips
that MegaSpeed imported could not be

71
00:04:41,735 --> 00:04:43,850
found in its data centers at all.

72
00:04:44,876 --> 00:04:47,926
Which brings us back to those sealed boxes in
Malaysia...

73
00:04:48,821 --> 00:04:54,433
After that discovery, MegaSpeed came onto the
radar of US agencies. Then Alice.

74
00:04:55,202 --> 00:04:59,983
According to reports, when surveillance began,
agents found she was close to an

75
00:04:59,983 --> 00:05:01,012
American citizen.

76
00:05:01,903 --> 00:05:03,737
That American was Jensen Huang.

77
00:05:04,754 --> 00:05:10,005
In October 2025, US intelligence officials
reportedly briefed President Trump about

78
00:05:10,005 --> 00:05:11,081
the relationship.

79
00:05:11,921 --> 00:05:17,560
In May 2026, Secretary of State Marco Rubio
reportedly warned Trump again, in a

80
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:17,917
memo.

81
00:05:18,724 --> 00:05:24,431
Then, on October 29th, 2026, the New York Times
broke the story to the world.

82
00:05:25,251 --> 00:05:28,673
At first, Nvidia and Jensen denied any
relationship.

83
00:05:29,460 --> 00:05:34,525
A few days later, Jensen sent a letter to his
employees. He admitted he had been

84
00:05:34,525 --> 00:05:37,628
unfaithful to his wife. He said he had no excuse.

85
00:05:38,242 --> 00:05:42,109
But the letter didn't mention Alice. And it didn't
mention spying.

86
00:05:42,932 --> 00:05:46,988
On November 11th, the New York Times reported that
Jensen had also had a

87
00:05:46,988 --> 00:05:49,467
relationship with a senior Nvidia executive.

88
00:05:50,181 --> 00:05:52,798
The next day, Reuters reported a third woman.

89
00:05:53,628 --> 00:05:55,559
Nvidia's stock was falling fast.

90
00:05:56,403 --> 00:06:02,134
And on the morning of November 12th, Jensen Huang
resigned from everything. CEO.

91
00:06:02,134 --> 00:06:03,639
President. The board.

92
00:06:04,560 --> 00:06:06,346
But the story didn't end there.

93
00:06:06,914 --> 00:06:12,359
A petition to bring him back collected more than
18,800 signatures. Big names,

94
00:06:12,359 --> 00:06:15,221
including Elon Musk, publicly backed him.

95
00:06:16,048 --> 00:06:21,448
On November 17th, Nvidia's board said clearly: he
is not coming back.

96
00:06:22,336 --> 00:06:27,127
Five days later, on November 22nd, the same board
voted unanimously to bring him

97
00:06:27,127 --> 00:06:29,583
back as CEO, president, and board member.

98
00:06:29,944 --> 00:06:35,217
The board said it had spoken with senior officials
in the US government, and was

99
00:06:35,217 --> 00:06:39,040
confident his return posed no threat to national
security.

100
00:06:39,909 --> 00:06:43,122
Earlier, according to reports, Jensen had told
Trump he had no idea Alice might be a

101
00:06:43,122 --> 00:06:45,379
spy. And Trump allegedly told him he should stay
on as CEO.

102
00:06:45,976 --> 00:06:49,302
Fired on the 12th. Back on the 22nd.

103
00:06:50,132 --> 00:06:51,243
Ten days.

104
00:06:51,811 --> 00:06:54,720
Now here is the part most people are missing.

105
00:06:55,732 --> 00:06:57,857
Is Alice Huang actually a Chinese spy?

106
00:06:58,492 --> 00:07:01,193
The honest answer: nobody has proven it.

107
00:07:02,034 --> 00:07:08,043
The US Attorney General, Todd Blanche, has said
the Justice Department has not

108
00:07:08,043 --> 00:07:11,510
reached a conclusion on whether she is a spy.

109
00:07:12,229 --> 00:07:17,021
And as of November 19th, the CIA was still saying
the intelligence so far could not

110
00:07:17,021 --> 00:07:18,176
prove it either way.

111
00:07:19,022 --> 00:07:23,758
Remember those public photos? Some people ask: if
she were a trained spy, why would

112
00:07:23,758 --> 00:07:28,095
her relationship with the most watched CEO in tech
be all over social media?

113
00:07:28,934 --> 00:07:30,847
So where did the spy story come from?

114
00:07:31,784 --> 00:07:35,539
To answer that, you have to look at a fight inside
the American government.

115
00:07:36,450 --> 00:07:41,514
On one side: Jensen Huang. He has said publicly,
many times, that he wants to sell

116
00:07:41,514 --> 00:07:46,640
more chips to China. And with his access to Trump,
some restrictions were loosened.

117
00:07:46,640 --> 00:07:51,705
Trump even allowed certain chip sales to China, if
Nvidia paid the US government a

118
00:07:51,705 --> 00:07:53,187
cut of 15 to 25 percent.

119
00:07:54,055 --> 00:07:58,956
On the other side: China hawks like Marco Rubio,
who strongly oppose selling chips

120
00:07:58,956 --> 00:07:59,494
to China.

121
00:08:00,328 --> 00:08:04,795
According to reports, it was Rubio's memo that
first labeled Alice a Chinese spy.

122
00:08:05,586 --> 00:08:10,935
But here's the twist. The CIA report behind that
memo reportedly never said she was

123
00:08:10,935 --> 00:08:14,157
a spy. That conclusion was Rubio's own assessment.

124
00:08:14,974 --> 00:08:16,776
So was this a real spy case?

125
00:08:17,656 --> 00:08:23,018
Or was a personal scandal turned into a weapon, in
a political war over who gets to

126
00:08:23,018 --> 00:08:24,310
sell chips to China?

127
00:08:25,555 --> 00:08:28,857
To see this clearly, you have to separate three
different issues.

128
00:08:29,744 --> 00:08:31,453
Issue one: conduct.

129
00:08:32,214 --> 00:08:37,308
Jensen admitted he cheated on his wife. But two of
the reported relationships were

130
00:08:37,308 --> 00:08:42,278
with Nvidia employees. When a CEO has
relationships with his own staff, that's a

131
00:08:42,278 --> 00:08:46,254
serious question of workplace ethics. That part is
not a theory.

132
00:08:47,519 --> 00:08:49,694
Issue two: conflict of interest.

133
00:08:50,517 --> 00:08:55,499
Spy or not, a company linked to the woman he was
involved with got Nvidia partner

134
00:08:55,499 --> 00:09:00,543
status and billions of dollars in chips. That is a
clear conflict of interest, and

135
00:09:00,543 --> 00:09:02,573
it deserves a full investigation.

136
00:09:03,538 --> 00:09:05,244
Issue three: the trade war.

137
00:09:06,108 --> 00:09:08,664
And this is where America's double standard shows.

138
00:09:09,391 --> 00:09:13,471
The US constantly tells other countries to open
their markets and remove trade

139
00:09:13,471 --> 00:09:17,499
barriers. It pressures countries like India to cut
tariffs on American goods.

140
00:09:18,252 --> 00:09:22,595
But when it comes to selling its own technology to
China, America shuts the door.

141
00:09:23,375 --> 00:09:25,749
Free trade, it seems, only goes one way.

142
00:09:26,683 --> 00:09:28,914
Now, the theory exploding online.

143
00:09:29,776 --> 00:09:32,034
Was this a way to move Nvidia's stock?

144
00:09:32,856 --> 00:09:37,280
The stock fell hard during the scandal, and jumped
sharply when Jensen came back.

145
00:09:37,280 --> 00:09:40,884
Anyone who bought at the bottom could have made a
fortune in days.

146
00:09:41,952 --> 00:09:47,354
But so far, no regulator, no court, and no major
outlet has accused anyone of market

147
00:09:47,354 --> 00:09:48,190
manipulation.

148
00:09:49,006 --> 00:09:55,233
Big swings like this usually get regulators
looking for unusual trades. If they find

149
00:09:55,233 --> 00:09:58,346
something, it will be a much bigger story.

150
00:09:58,863 --> 00:10:02,623
And one more open question: exactly who leaked the
story, and why at that moment, is

151
00:10:02,623 --> 00:10:03,652
still not fully public.

152
00:10:04,626 --> 00:10:06,033
So here is our forecast.

153
00:10:06,988 --> 00:10:12,791
Jensen Huang stays CEO through 2027. The board,
Washington, and investors all want

154
00:10:12,791 --> 00:10:13,499
him there.

155
00:10:14,333 --> 00:10:18,221
But the fight over chips to China does not go
away. It gets louder.

156
00:10:19,095 --> 00:10:20,369
Watch three signals.

157
00:10:21,265 --> 00:10:26,324
One: whether the CIA or the Justice Department
ever reaches a final conclusion about

158
00:10:26,324 --> 00:10:27,047
Alice Huang.

159
00:10:27,934 --> 00:10:33,366
Two: what happens to MegaSpeed, and whether anyone
is charged over the missing

160
00:10:33,366 --> 00:10:33,784
chips.

161
00:10:34,593 --> 00:10:38,926
Three: the next decision on chip sales to China.
Because whoever wins that fight,

162
00:10:38,926 --> 00:10:42,671
Jensen's camp or the hawks, will tell you who
really won this scandal.

163
00:10:43,151 --> 00:10:45,315
Now I want to hear from you.

164
00:10:46,732 --> 00:10:47,804
Real spy case, or political weapon?

165
00:10:48,619 --> 00:10:50,834
Tell me your forecast in the comments.

166
00:10:51,801 --> 00:10:57,884
And if you want to see what's coming before it
hits the headlines, subscribe to The

167
00:10:57,884 --> 00:10:59,130
Crimson Forecast.

168
00:11:00,211 --> 00:11:02,953
This file is closed. See you in the next one.
